WEBVTT

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.650
Wh-What is that?

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.160
H-How is it moving?!

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.700
Bearabbit.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.660
<i>Okay, bear!</i>

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.270
<i>Ladies and gentlemen!</i>

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.210
I am...

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.160
a god!

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.240
Everyone!

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.930
Watch closely!

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.980
Wha?!

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.980
Th-The obelisk disappeared?!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.830
Well? Impressive, isn't it?

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:50.210
Now, here's a gift from God Akatsuki!

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.500
That's...

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.710
Mayonnaise!

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.480
Good!

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.220
It's really good!

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.980
Now, everyone, have faith in God Akatsuki!

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.730
Those who worship him and
have faith shall find salvation!

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.460
This is the power of a god!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.390
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.130
<b>It Seems Akatsuki's
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hBecoming God Akatsuki!</b>

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.740
Man, business just picked up!

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.340
Yes, it did.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.800
Hmm? What's the matter?

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.710
To be honest, I haven't been able 
to thank Tsukasa for saving me yet.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.640
Oh, really?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:28.200
Now, everyone, worship your god!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.370
Worship me!

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.000
Worship me!

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.930
I can't believe Akatsuki's our god.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.760
I thought it would be best

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.650
to use the power of religion if 
we hope to unite the region.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.390
Declaring ourselves a nation wouldn't
be enough to win over the people.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.050
Thus the magic show, huh?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:45.760
Yeah.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.550
A religion will be easy 
for them to understand.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.880
Also, portraying ourselves 
as a god and his messengers

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.190
will enable a smooth transfer of power

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.690
to the people of this world 
when we do return to our own.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.190
I see.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.800
We're also calling ours the Seven-Light Faith.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.340
We might eventually be contacted 
by someone who knows the real one.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.280
Oh, so that's the Ruruck Mountain Range.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.130
Are we really going?

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.120
Of course we're going.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.250
I have to get information 
on Buchwald, after all.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.480
It's snowing a lot, though.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.920
No problem, no problem.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.160
The world's top journalist isn't 
about to lose to a little snow.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.720
Now, let's go, El!

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.140
Y-Yeah.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.490
It's Akatsuki and the others 
from the Seven-Light Faith.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:56.000
Attention, everyone, 
we have a gift from Akatsuki!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.780
It's mayo time!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.620
I'll follow you forever, Lord Akatsuki!

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:03.420
Me, too!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.250
Me, too!

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.410
Seven-Light Faith!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.570
Seven-Light Faith!

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.010
Seven-Light Faith! Seven-Light Faith!

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.570
Dormundt is finished.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.700
I need to escape with my family
as soon as possible.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.360
Come in.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.210
I'm leaving here tomorrow morning.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.660
Prepare my things...

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.410
And where do you think
you're going, Mayor Haizerad?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.160
Y-You're...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.950
of the Seven-Light Faith?!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.670
Mikogami Tsukasa, one of the angels
serving God Akatsuki.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.670
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.560
I came here to talk.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.180
I had a feeling you had 
the wrong idea about us.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.810
Wrong idea?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:03.310
We haven't come here to persecute 
nobles or throw this city into chaos.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:08.050
In fact, we'd like to cooperate 
with you and the nobility.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:12.450
After all, there's work that 
only you all can handle.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.700
Of course, we'll guarantee a fair wage for you.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:20.730
Or would you prefer to flee
 to some unknown land,

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:25.340
exhausting the scant assets you take as
you live in fear of both us and the empire?

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.630
What are you asking me to do?

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:32.730
Would you continue serving 
as Mayor of Dormundt

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:37.020
and show allegiance to us 
and the Seven-Light Faith?

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.860
Mayor Haizerad has an announcement?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.200
Why is he with the Seven-Light Faith?

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.560
What's going to happen to Dormundt?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.760
I am the Mayor of Dormundt, 
Walter Von Haizerad.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.670
Here today I henceforth proclaim

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:13.750
that this city shall be governed 
by the Seven-Light Faith!

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:35.700
Seven-Light Faith!

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:30.680
I'm glad.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:31.940
Tell me about it.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:38.700
What is this?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.710
Right?

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.950
It looks so good on him, it's kind of creepy.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.320
My, I think he looks cute and lovely.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.960
I-Indeed.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.570
Besides, in order for Tsukasa

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:51.930
to sneak into the H-Haizerad mansion 
without raising suspicion,

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:56.150
h-he had no choice but to disguise himself so.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.850
<b>On
{|fscx90}Reconnaissance</b>

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.320
Also, this one's...

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.930
A low-angle shot...

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.080
He's wearing his suit underneath?

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.110
Yes.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.250
Th-This...

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.840
U-Um, um...

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.110
I'll send it to you later.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.610
Th-Thank you.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:23.050
If you all are enjoying it this much, 
then it was worth disguising myself.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.630
So, what do we do now?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.750
We've united Findolf, but...

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:31.370
Yeah. I'll focus on domestic affairs 
here in Dormundt for a while,

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.280
and shore up our foundation.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:37.040
You all can return to 
Elm Village and get some rest.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.220
I've worked you all too hard
for the last few days.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.020
Thank God.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.430
I'm all worn out already.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.440
It's been a while since 
we were in Elm Village.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.690
Hmmm? What's the matter, Keine?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.330
I have a small request.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.040
Okay, what is it?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.080
We're running low on medical supplies,

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:59.530
so I'd like a facility to produce antibiotics.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.200
Could you spare me some labor and capital?

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.700
Of course I don't mind doing that,

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.460
but are you sure you don't need any rest?

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.790
Yes.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:11.340
Compared to the battlefield, 
things have been relaxed here.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.650
All right.

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.960
Then get me a list of what you'll need,

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.240
and I'll have it arranged.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.640
Thank you.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:22.350
Aoi, I'd like you to stay with 
Akatsuki while you take your break.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.250
Understood.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.550
I shall remain at his side 
and protect him at all times.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:30.600
Hey, at least leave me alone while 
I bathe and use the bathroom!

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.600
I will not!

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.360
Wha?!

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.070
Also, Ringo.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.300
We're starting to run low on electricity.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.200
I'd like to have a new power station,

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.870
though a small-scale one is fine.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:48.660
I-If you're okay with thermal power, 
I-I can get that ready in no time.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.350
That's fine.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.290
Merchant can get you any materials you need.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.520
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:59.130
We've got plenty of money right now,
so I'll get you anything.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.590
Oh, right, Tsukasa.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.300
Hmm?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.530
There are quite a few soldiers

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:09.390
between those from Findolf Castle 
and the Dormundt watch,

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.330
but what's your plan?

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:15.610
Yeah, I'm thinking of combining them into 
a Seven-Light Faith Knight Order.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.900
You'll need a leader, then.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.120
I have an idea for that.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.690
There's one man I would absolutely 
love to entrust that to.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.160
Hey, did you hear?

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.670
The entire watch is being incorporated 
into the Seven-Light Faith.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.600
Yeah,

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.910
I heard we'll get better 
pay than before, too.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.080
Wow, really?

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.560
I'm out.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:43.450
Huh?

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.180
C-Captain?!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.480
May I join you?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.610
You're the angel...

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.430
I'm Mikogami Tsukasa.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.610
Feel free to call me Tsukasa.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.600
You would be the Silver Knight, 
Zest Do Bernard, correct?

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.370
You're right, that's my name.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:17.320
Though only Imperial Knights get to 
have "Do" added onto their names.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:21.010
So that doesn't fit who I am anymore.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.720
Well then, Bernard.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.640
I took the liberty of looking into you.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.260
You've demonstrated great courage,

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.150
your fellow soldiers have great trust in you,

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:35.080
and you're a reliable man, capable of 
making calm judgments at all times.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.110
I'm honored by all your praise.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.740
So what did you need from me?

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.340
There's something I'd like 
to ask of you.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.270
About our order of knights...

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.900
Order of knights?

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:53.750
Sorry, but I've already left the watch.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.120
Oh? Why is that?

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.250
Because you all have come here.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.800
What do you mean?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:07.440
You all seem relieved 
after taking over Findolf

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.720
with your mayonnaise and your divine power,

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.370
but the empire will come attack you.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.230
This place will become a battlefield.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:23.110
There's also something 
else that I have to do.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.830
If I can't do that, then there's 
no point in being a knight.

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:28.660
So I'm quitting.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:35.050
Choosing your own job is a part of 
this democracy you're propagating, right?

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.420
So, sorry, forget about me.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.010
How'd it go?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.600
With your candidate for head knight?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.950
He was exactly the kind 
of man I thought he'd be.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.060
But he said he's stepping down as a knight.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.770
Huh? What's that mean?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.360
So what's the plan now?

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.500
No problem.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.210
I'll just go talk to him again tomorrow.

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.150
You came all the way out here?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:29.500
What do you need, angel?

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.960
I hadn't yet had the chance 
to discuss the key issue.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.380
Key issue?

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:38.810
We would like you to be 
the leader of our knights.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.160
Huh? I already told you, didn't I?

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.440
I'm done being a knight.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.110
We would still like to ask it of you.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.820
I'm more certain than ever after yesterday.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.320
I believe we need a man like you.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.110
Listen, angel...

00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.880
Papa!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:01.820
Airi?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.040
What's the matter?

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.780
I thought you were going out.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:10.840
I missed you, so I came back.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.840
Oh, really?

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.960
I missed you too, Airi!

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:16.270
Yay!

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.350
Your daughter?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.560
That's right!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.360
Papa's my papa!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:25.400
She's the precious treasure left to me 
by my wife, who passed away in an epidemic.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:30.110
Airi, Papa's having a discussion 
with this young man.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.640
Could you go play over there for a bit?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.550
Yeah, okay!

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:42.150
Angel, I served as a knight 
so I could live with Airi.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:46.880
There's nothing more precious 
to me than my daughter.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.800
So I'm willing to do anything if 
it means I can live with her.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:54.890
But I can't make any choices 
that would sacrifice my family.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.890
If it means I'll be sent off to fight
when this town becomes a battlefield,

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.350
or that I won't be able to live with Airi,

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.670
then I have no reason to remain a knight.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.540
That's the only reason I ever became 
a knight in the first place.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:12.240
There are plenty of other 
knights with great loyalty

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:15.790
who do it for the empire or the emperor.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.060
So I don't think a pathetic man like me

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.370
would be good a fit for the 
leader of a nation's order.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:26.880
What makes you say cherishing your 
family above all else is pathetic?

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.630
Bernard, you're perfectly welcome

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.060
to continue putting your 
daughter first and foremost.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:38.640
What we're seeking isn't loyalty.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.970
It's companions who will fight alongside us.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:42.520
Companions?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.620
We're not like the rulers 
you've known before us.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:51.230
Our goal is to create a democratic nation
where everyone can live free.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.820
I'm sure you've had these thoughts before:

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:58.730
"It's not right for heritage 
and other unreasonable factors

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.100
to determine whose life has value
when we're all the same."

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:05.490
We aim to destroy that world.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:08.400
But to do that, we'll need people like you

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:11.840
to change the way
you've lived and thought before.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.570
We'll need you all to take 
part in the revolution.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.770
After all, it won't be a 
real people's revolution

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:23.020
if you, the people, don't have the 
drive to shape this world yourselves.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:29.370
Are you saying you can really
create a world where everyone

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.150
is free to decide their future for themselves?

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.900
With your help, we can.

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:45.300
What is a knight?

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.220
What is a sword?

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:52.260
Is a knight not someone who fights 
to protect what's truly important?

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:57.160
Is a sword not a tool wielded by those knights
to protect what's precious to them?

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.760
Bernard,

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.810
if you'd like to stay with those you love,

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:07.640
then we'd like you to once more, of your
own free will, choose to be a knight

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:10.680
and show the world as the 
leader of our knights

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:14.980
that the future belongs to each and 
every individual living on this earth.

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:28.410
I suppose it might be a better
to fight to seize our own future

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.110
when the empire attacks us anyways.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:37.290
I, Zest Bernard, shall dedicate 
myself to this huge responsibility.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.570
We'll be counting on you.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.850
That silver-haired brat!

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.140
Angel, my foot! Sounds shady!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.850
You've drank too much.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.810
He'll hear you.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.610
Huh?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:01.820
I don't care if he hears me.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.300
<i>Nobles, huh?</i>

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:08.750
<i>I expected some opposition there.</i>

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.080
<i>However, I'll need to keep an eye 
on their behavior moving forward.</i>

00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:16.920
What?!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.840
Findolf was attacked by a rebel army?!

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.760
I-Is that true?!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.830
Yeah.

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.530
We heard it from a knight 
who fled, so it must be.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.850
Scary!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.890
Do you think they'll come here, too?

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.990
Y-You'll be fine.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:35.690
That's what we're here for, after all.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:39.480
Besides, there's more than just 
us Buchwald soldiers here.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:43.760
We have a large army from Arclide, 
and the main knight unit here, too.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:47.790
So once spring comes,
we'll blow that rebel army away!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.040
Wow! That's so good to hear!

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:57.480
But, you know, Duke Fastidious 
is telling us to go right now.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:01.970
When you say Duke Fastidious, 
do you mean the lord of Gustave?

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:05.080
Uh-huh. He's an incredible man.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.470
His martial prowess is amazing,
but so is his magic.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.640
During the last battle with the Yamato Empire,

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.750
he stood on the front 
lines himself firing away.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.100
It was the first time in history

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:19.820
that a knight was granted the 
title of Duke and the authority

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.610
to govern the northern lands.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.550
Amazing!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.160
It is.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.770
He swore absolute loyalty to the emperor,

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:31.250
and now he's a merciless perfectionist 
to those who oppose the emperor's will.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:32.750
Wow!

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:37.350
I didn't know Lord Gustave was 
such an incredible person!

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.630
She's taking her time coming back.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.970
Oh, you're back, Elch.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:49.770
When did you?!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.980
Did you hear anything interesting?

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.600
Not at all.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.730
It's all talk about how they're going 
to march on Findolf once winter passes.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.120
I see.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.900
How about you?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:07.240
Well, I heard there's this amazing mage,
a special mage officer.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:10.240
Oh, you mean Gustave, Duke Fastidious?

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:12.320
But while people say he's incredible,

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:16.250
there's not much information
about how good he actually is.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.740
Hmm...

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.400
Okay, I've decided!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.000
Huh?

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:24.090
Let's go meet this Duke Fastidious 
they're talking about!

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.620
Go meet him?

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:30.760
What?!

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:35.760
P-Please, gracious Gustave,

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:39.400
I-I would like to request your aid 
in restoring the land of Findolf.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:44.400
You are a proud imperial knight, 
and yet you've shamelessly clung to life?

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:57.020
Those damn rebels...

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:03.460
I, Oslo El Gustave,
shall burn them all to the ground.
